LavaRnd version 0.2.1

    13-Nov-2026

    Fixed lavapool hanging when its camera is unplugged.  The kernel
    reports an unplugged V4L2 camera to select() as an exception, and
    lavapool answered that by quietly closing the camera and carrying
    on with no source: it served what was left in its pool, then timed
    out every client.  It now logs the reason and exits, so systemd
    restarts it, and it comes back once the camera is plugged in again.
    Tested by unplugging a QuickCam Pro 4000 on a Raspberry Pi.

LavaRnd version 0.2.0

    13-Nov-2026

    First release of the revival fork at github.com/kbresin/lavarnd.
    It is not an upstream release; see README.md and PORTING.md for
    the reasons behind each change.  It builds and runs on Linux
    (tested on Rocky 9 x86-64 and Debian 13 aarch64).

    Incompatible changes from 0.1.3:

	Removed the Perl API (perllib), the Perl trickle and the Perl
	test.  A Python library and a Python trickle replace them.

	Removed the V4L1 ov511 camera driver.  Linux no longer has V4L1.

	`make install` is now a systemd system install: lavapool and
	trickle run as unprivileged dynamic users, with programs in
	/usr/local/sbin and configuration in /etc/LavaRnd.  The old
	per-directory install rules, the lava account setup and the
	LavaRnd.rc init script are gone.  `make uninstall` reverses it.

    Cameras:

	Ported the pwc driver (QuickCam Pro 4000 and relatives) from
	V4L1 to V4L2, and recalibrated its camsanity limits.

	Added a uvc driver for ordinary USB webcams, with a calibrated
	preset for the Logitech C270 and a generic preset.

	lavapool now notices when the camera is unplugged and exits, so
	systemd restarts it once the camera is back.

    Python:

	Added a pure-Python client library (python/) that talks to
	lavapool directly, including a random.Random subclass.
	Retries are spaced out so clients survive a lavapool restart.

	Rewrote trickle in Python.  It can credit entropy to the
	kernel with RNDADDENTROPY (-e BITS) when it has CAP_SYS_ADMIN.

    Build:

	The build is warning-free with -Wall -Werror on gcc 11 and on
	Debian 13's gcc, which fixed real bugs: callback pointers were
	truncated to int, pselect() got the wrong time struct, and the
	system_stuff hash covered the pointer instead of the struct.

	Shared libraries are linked with cc, so aarch64 picks up libgcc.

	camsanity statistics were fixed and it now stops cleanly.

    Added examples/dice, a small Flask app that rolls dice with LavaRnd.

LavaRnd version 0.1.3

    15-Nov-2003

    Fixed a few more compile warnings reported by users when they
    compiled the LavaRnd source on different architectures.

    Added camsanity values for a Logitech QuickCam Pro 4000 from
    Martin Kretschmar (mail at martin dash kretschmar dot de).
    We used the 500 frame run where he had just rebooted and
    plugged in the camera.

    Adjusted the camsanity for the pwc730 after reports from some
    users that recently purchased cameras failed against the older
    sanity checks.

LavaRnd version 0.1.2

    09-Nov-2003

    Fixed a number of compile warnings reported by users when they
    compiled the LavaRnd source on different architectures.

LavaRnd version 0.1.1

    25-Aug-2003

    Make install, after other directories are installed (and in particular
    the lib directory is installed), will clobber and rebuild the perllib
    directory before installing it.  Hopefully this will provide a
    work-around for the "Perl modules do not load: 2003-08-17" bug.

    Fixed the output of pwc_print() and ov511_print() in regards to
    printing of sanity values.  This fixes the sanity value output of
    tool such as camget, camset, etc.

    Added comments to the imgtally output so that people will use the
    Shannon entropy measurements instead of the Chi^2 bit variation
    guesses.  Since camsanity produces good entropy estimates, the
    TODO item related to a missing entropy was removed.

    Recommend that people use:

    	camset cam_type cam_device -L -v 1

    to output the default LavaRnd configuration.

=-=

